<title>SINGAPORE: DBS Bank 1996 net profit up 12.6 pct.</title>
<headline>DBS Bank 1996 net profit up 12.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    669.45 vs   594.64</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)		8.00 vs     8.00</p>
<p>    Preferential dividend (cents)     3.00 vs     2.25</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    97.00 vs    88.00</p>
<p>    Group interest income (blns)	2.38 vs     2.13</p>
<p>    Group interest expense (blns)     1.52 vs     1.34</p>
<p>    Group net interest income	 863.31 vs   783.17</p>
<p>    Group fees and commissions	256.91 vs   232.24</p>
<p>    Group dividends			77.32 vs    73.67</p>
<p>    Group rental			   31.96 vs    32.21</p>
<p>    Group other income		  159.57 vs   126.91</p>
<p>    Group operating expenses	  468.35 vs   417.01</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		836.14 vs   766.58</p>
<p>    Group tax			     166.05 vs   172.48</p>
<p>    Group minorities	     (gain) 0.64 vs   0.53 (loss)</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: June 2, 1997</p>
<p>Last day register open: May 19, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Analysts had expected The Development Bank of Singapore Ltd to report a 13 percent rise in group net profit to around Singapore $670 million. Estimates had varied between S$624.0 million and S$691.1 million.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
